{%- comment -%}
  Buybox Header
  Displays: SKU, title, reviews.

  @param modal - true inside the Quick Shop modal. The collection page already
                 owns the page's <h1>, so the title drops to a <p> styled the
                 same, and the reviews link points at the product page's review
                 widget instead of an anchor that does not exist here.
{%- endcomment -%}

{%- assign current_variant = current_variant | default: product.selected_or_first_available_variant -%}
{%- if modal -%}
  {%- assign reviews_href = product.url | append: '#product-reviews-widget' -%}
{%- else -%}
  {%- assign reviews_href = '#product-reviews-widget' -%}
{%- endif -%}

{%- comment -%}
  Products with no reviews rendered an empty "☆☆☆☆☆ 0 Reviews" row, so the
  widget is only mounted once Yotpo reports at least one review. The count is
  read off the metafield Yotpo syncs per product; `.value` covers the metafield
  drop and the bare fallback covers the legacy shape, and `times: 1` turns
  either (or a missing metafield) into a number we can compare.
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- assign yotpo_review_count = product.metafields.yotpo.review_count.value
  | default: product.metafields.yotpo.review_count
  | times: 1
-%}

<div class="buybox-header">
  {%- comment -%}
    The mobile collection line used to sit here, printing
    product.collections.first. That is whichever collection Shopify happens to
    return first, so it surfaced internal ones ("BC All", "Artistry in
    Mosaics") rather than the series — and the breadcrumbs above already name
    the series on mobile, so the line was redundant even when it was right.
  {%- endcomment -%}

  {%- comment -%} Title block: Desktop = SKU above title, Mobile = title above SKU (via CSS order) {%- endcomment -%}
  <div class="buybox-title-block">
    {%- if current_variant.sku != blank -%}
      <p class="buybox-sku" data-sku>SKU: {{ current_variant.sku }}</p>
    {%- endif -%}
    {%- if modal -%}
      <p class="buybox-title">
        <a href="{{ product.url }}">{{ product.title }}</a>
      </p>
    {%- else -%}
      <h1 class="buybox-title">{{ product.title }}</h1>
    {%- endif -%}
  </div>

  {%- comment -%} Yotpo star rating + reviews count — only once there is one {%- endcomment -%}
  {%- if yotpo_review_count > 0 -%}
    <a class="yotpo-link buybox-reviews" href="{{ reviews_href }}">
      <div
        class="yotpo-widget-instance"
        data-yotpo-instance-id="593213"
        data-yotpo-product-id="{{ product.id }}"
        data-yotpo-cart-product-id="{{ product.id }}"
        data-yotpo-section-id="{{ template.name }}"
      ></div>
    </a>
  {%- endif -%}
</div>
